<title>FRANCE: Fire forces French N-power station to scale down.</title>
<headline>Fire forces French N-power station to scale down.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>A fire at a central France nuclear power station has forced the plant to scale down its operations, officials said on Saturday.</p>
<p>The transformer fire in a non-nuclear section of the Dampierre-en-Burly station in the Loiret department on Friday night was quickly brought under control.</p>
<p>The fire caused a large explosion, forcing the power station to reduce its overall operations.</p>
<p>Plant management said repairs could take several weeks.</p>
